.TH geectl-build-buildinfo 1  "geectl-build-buildinfo 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-build\-buildinfo \- Read the buildinfo for a package: the blocking error, if any, and the dependencies the build pulls in
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl build buildinfo\fR [\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> <\fIPACKAGE\fR> <\fIREPOSITORY\fR> <\fIARCH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read the buildinfo for a package: the blocking error, if any, and the dependencies the build pulls in
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-alternative\-project\fR \fI<ALTERNATIVE_PROJECT>\fR
Read the buildinfo for another project instead of `project`: the dep set the package would build against there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project the package is in
.TP
<\fIPACKAGE\fR>
The package to read the buildinfo for
.TP
<\fIREPOSITORY\fR>
The repository the package builds in
.TP
<\fIARCH\fR>
The architecture the package builds for
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
